  "scope": "Three public requests at seed 8102. Roof-on exterior, sampled functional room groups and secondary cutaway. This is comparison evidence, not the full house-style acceptance matrix.",
  "findings": [
    "Warm earth-coloured walls give a distinct palette, but the roof reads as broad golden courses rather than a convincing local thatch assembly.",
    "The narrowed fictional savanna household brief is not expressed by room sequence or household material choices. Small/default/large use cottage-like rectangles and partitions.",
    "The default parlour is a long bench against a bare wall; the large parlour remains mostly empty floor with a bench and cupboard.",
    "Kitchens use the same rough metal-banded bench and metal pot, with generic bottles, shelves and barrels.",
    "Sleeping rooms repeat the same raised single bed, chest and nightstand as the other styles; little privacy or fitted comfort is legible.",
    "The three scales have no strong shaded social threshold or relation between gathering, cooking and the exterior. Do not equate the API label with cultural authenticity."
  ],
